            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 5. It is the present intention of the parties that the plan of pension benefits will be so determined with the advice of an actuary that the contributions will be sufficient, (1) to meet such reasonable expenses as may be incurred in the development and operation of the Plan, (2) to meet the current costs of benefits accruing under the Plan, and (3) ultimately to fund the past service costs within a period of thirty (30) years.",
